      "writtenOn": "2019-05-22T17:03:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Reading the RISC manual, I am a little fuzzy on how rd works. From this code it looks like it is always the result of the initial read of rs1 (*addr), but the instruction set manual text makes me think rd could also how the result of the operation of rs1 AND rs2, which would always be 0 in this case. Can you confirm that ret is actually return the previous value please?\n\n\n\"These AMO instructions atomically load a data value from the address in rs1, place the value into register rd, apply a binary operator to the loaded value and the original value in rs2, then store the result back to the address in rs1.\"\n\nThe above text is what I am going off of. I can convince myself either way of the value of rd to being the original rs1 value or the post rs1 value (but I am now leaning towards it holding the original rs1 value - so your implementation would be correct)",
